				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-29T19:56:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@noleli\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>noleli</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> A good site has a `sitemap.xml` file, right?! 😅</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111495617132402695",
			"parentId": "111495596680463031",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh/111495616834289238",
			"author": {
				"name": "Khalid ⚡",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-29T20:01:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@noleli\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>noleli</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I like the suggested idea of generating a page with “randomish” links that might be hidden, and then the client randomizes a redirect. You can even use local storage to keep it so the random algorithm doesn’t suggest the same links more than a few times within a particular period.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111495634289387287",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong/111495634013012614",
			"author": {
				"name": "Cory Birdsong",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/543/551/045/998/536/original/e10f042a7b2e4a2e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-29T20:06:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Collect all the URLs on the site in a big Javascript array, plop that on the page, then pick one randomly and window.open() it? It would cause two full page loads in a row, but you could put a fun spinner on the “random\" page to make that feel less bad.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111495658841551193",
			"parentId": "111495634289387287",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong/111495658628095798",
			"author": {
				"name": "Cory Birdsong",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/543/551/045/998/536/original/e10f042a7b2e4a2e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-29T20:12:16.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Thinking about it, a client-side solution would also be a reasonable choice on a Wordpress site? Lots of hosts cache all queries for performance reasons, in which case `’orderby' =&gt; 'rand’` would go to the same page repeatedly until the cache gets purged. If you disabled caching specifically for /random it could still slow down the site overall since every visit to the page would result in an expensive database query.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
