		{
			"id": "111495887401018889",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mstrkapowski/111495887374583642",
			"author": {
				"name": "https://chrismcleod.dev",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mstrkapowski",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/294/555/739/927/762/original/4564fa21b77ba437.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-29T21:10:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> My first thought was to generate an array of every post in the site at build time, and insert it into a /random/index.html page that runs some JS to pick a random value to redirect to. It’s not pretty, but it should run pretty much everywhere. You could spice it up by remembering posts the visitor has read and filtering those from the array.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
